From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:20:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] tccgen: fold calls to trivial static functions

A static (inline or not) function whose body is "{ }", "{ return
<constant>; }" or, for a void function, "{ if (<constant 0>) <stmt> }"
is folded at its direct call sites, as an optimizing compiler does
after inlining: the arguments are still evaluated, then dropped, and
the constant is pushed; the function is not referenced.  The Linux
kernel relies on that for its IS_ENABLED()-style stubs, whose callers
reference symbols of the disabled subsystem.

The return expression is probed by parsing it for real with the
parameters in scope and nocode_wanted set; side effects (stores,
helper calls, volatile reads, calls that are not folded) are detected
while parsing at the probe's own nesting level, so dead arms of ?:, &&
and || and sizeof do not count.  This folds transitively ("return 0 ||
f(x)" with f folded) and through ({ ... }) expressions.  Names
starting with "__builtin_" are known; nothing is probed with -g.

The fold is tied to the defining symbol (its token is kept in the
function type's "c" field): other symbols sharing the type, such as a
weak alias "extern __typeof(dummy) __stdio_exit __attribute__((weak,
alias("dummy")))" which the link may resolve to a real function, keep
their calls.  The result lives in FuncAttr (func_fold, func_fval; the
func_used bit is reserved for the following patch).
---
 tcc.h    |   4 +-
 tccgen.c | 189 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 189 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tcc.h b/tcc.h
index 0937dfb..003a707 100644
--- a/tcc.h
+++ b/tcc.h
@@ -521,7 +521,9 @@ struct FuncAttr {
     func_dtor   : 1, /* attribute((destructor)) */
     func_args   : 8, /* PE __stdcall args */
     func_alwinl : 1, /* always_inline */
-    xxxx        : 15;
+    func_fold   : 2, /* trivial body: 1 empty (void), 2 'return <const>' */
+    func_fval   : 12, /* the constant + 2048 (see inline_fold_check) */
+    func_used   : 1; /* attribute((used)) */
 };
 
 /* symbol management */
diff --git a/tccgen.c b/tccgen.c
index bf17656..717d822 100644
--- a/tccgen.c
+++ b/tccgen.c
@@ -161,9 +161,11 @@ static void gen_inline_functions(TCCState *s);
